                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd6dca8c-429a-34f5-9652-63b9be7b5831",
                        "entry_id": "94f2b696-4d23-3f53-ab39-d2602bdab6e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Übergang vom Rachen zur Luftröhre"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5428532-7908-4c43-b9db-66c134a8699c",
                                "sense_id": "dd6dca8c-429a-34f5-9652-63b9be7b5831",
                                "text": "Der Larynx wies Zeichen einer Erkrankung auf."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2838a03a-c5b9-4b47-9734-b8cca8abd8fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "94f2b696-4d23-3f53-ab39-d2602bdab6e4",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd6dca8c-429a-34f5-9652-63b9be7b5831",
                        "source_sense_description": "Übergang vom Rachen zur Luftröhre",
                        "target_lang_word": "larynx",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "larynx",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                        "entry_id": "0269197b-749f-31a0-88b2-b967895002d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hollow muscular organ of the neck of mammals situated just below where the tract of the pharynx splits into the trachea and the oesophagus. It is involved in breath control and protection of the trachea, and, as it houses the vocal cords, sound production."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abb1375e-f312-469c-8969-680c7bd8148d",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "There is one thing, among abundance of others, in Anatomy, which has always much affected me with Admiration, [...] It is the Situation and Elaſticity of the Epiglottis, a ſoft Cartilaginous Cover to the Larynx, or Orifice of the Wind-pipe; that this Epiglottis ſhould, all a Man's life, be drawn up, for the Benefit of Reſpiration, and fall down and ſhut, whilſt every bit we eat, and every drop we drink, paſſes over it into the Gullet and Stomach; and that we ſhould ſo ſeldom have Occaſion to cough up a crum, or drop, that may accidentaly ſlip into the Larynx; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e61e6ad2-ab1f-43e6-8a3e-eb7b6814bc87",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "The larynx is the instrument of the voice, of which the rima glottidis is the immediate organ. [...] The change of the voice from acute to grave at the time of puberty, when the larynx undergoes a remarkable development, as well as its acuteness in females, whose glottis is less by one third than that of man, shew that the size of the aperture has a great influence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd0c69d4-3daa-46dd-a374-77fa5313b50a",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "The differences in the voices of man and woman cannot but have been always obſerved; and their larynxes exhibit, on a merely ſuperficial inſpection, a great diſproportion in ſize."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0983275f-2586-49e4-9bff-9dddbfb7b03b",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "I hope to be understood as not implying that there is no peculiarity of the larynges and tracheæ, except in some genera; for I believe all have the admirable mechanism of the organ of voice differently constructed, with corresponding muscles, and distribution of nerves, producing those various modulations of sound so familiar to us, and destined for the excitement of love, as well as for other purposes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53157bc6-66d7-409e-aba6-8590e6fc6799",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "The work on larynx transplantation has been discussed in the previous paragraphs. Corollary to this is the possible development of an artificial larynx which can be implanted just as an artificial heart might be implanted. Design of such larynxes might permit a quick solution to the problem of tissue rejection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b28e56e6-6248-415e-b391-be3630cc64e0",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "The ability of Red Deer stags to lower their larynx when roaring appears to be one of the exaggerators of formant dispersal, since the resting position of the male larynx is already lower than the typical mammalian position. [...] Size exaggeration provides an intriguing, non-linguistic explanation for the descent of the human larynx [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "966627a6-6a31-4aa9-b8ed-1375cc49dc78",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ba8846-7f78-3b8b-a945-ba5bc4d297cb",
                                                "text": "Study of intubated larynges from infants of 22 to 40 weeks' gestation who survived a few hours to 300 days showed acute injury was almost invariable, and up to 100% of the subglottic epithelium was lost within a few hour of intubation, but progression of injury was relatively short-lived."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a8be0cc-b504-460d-9b87-61ad7542af6a",
                        "source_entry_id": "94f2b696-4d23-3f53-ab39-d2602bdab6e4",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd6dca8c-429a-34f5-9652-63b9be7b5831",
                        "source_sense_description": "Übergang vom Rachen zur Luftröhre",
                        "target_lang_word": "larynx",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "larynx",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f2f37d6-47f0-3913-ab9e-13fc9ba1bc09",
                                        "entry_id": "0cd13093-8306-3c54-bcd0-c2aa86f84737",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partie supérieure de la trachée-artère, qui est un des organes de la respiration et le principal instrument de la voix."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6821057-2ab1-4265-9c92-4151d45d5fc5",
                                                "sense_id": "1f2f37d6-47f0-3913-ab9e-13fc9ba1bc09",
                                                "text": "Le larynx n’est pas fixe à l’intérieur du cou : il se déplace de haut en bas lors de la phonation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "469fa37d-c28e-411d-b8c3-e0ca2343a3b9",
                                                "sense_id": "1f2f37d6-47f0-3913-ab9e-13fc9ba1bc09",
                                                "text": "Dans le premier cas il s'agissait d'un blessé dont le larynx fut traversé par une balle; on fit une trachéotomie pour des accidents respiratoires inquiétants, puis on décanula le malade quelques jours après sans pratiquer un examen du larynx."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4f625bc-d7c4-477f-aad9-48cda2028ec6",
                                                "sense_id": "1f2f37d6-47f0-3913-ab9e-13fc9ba1bc09",
                                                "text": "Ce qui serait cool, c'est que tu te mettes à fumer, et peut-être que d'ici 30 ans tu auras un cancer du larynx et je ne t'entendrai plus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
